  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between Cocosamide B and Thrombopoietin through a series of molecular interactions. Cocosamide B is implicated in targeting Tankyrase-2, which is a target of (3R)-5,8,9-trimethoxy-2,2-dimethyl-3,4-dihydropyrano[2,3-b]quinolin-3-ol, and this compound further targets Thrombopoietin. Similarly, Cocosamide B is also shown to target HepG2, which is a target of the same compound, and this compound again targets Thrombopoietin. Additionally, Cocosamide B is linked to VMRC-LCP, which is a target of 6-C-Methylquercetin 3-methyl ether, which also targets Thrombopoietin. These findings collectively indicate that Cocosamide B may act through a common pathway involving the compound (3R)-5,8,9-trimethoxy-2,2-dimethyl-3,4-dihydropyrano[2,3-b]quinolin-3-ol, which ultimately leads to the activation of Thrombopoietin. The evidence suggests a possible mechanism where Cocosamide B influences the expression or activity of downstream targets that ultimately affect Thrombopoietin, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated."
